==English==

===Etymology===
1718, "untrustful, suspicious", either from {{suffix|en|leer|y}}, {{suffix|en|lear|t1=learning, knowledge|y}}. More at {{l|en|leer}}, {{l|en|lear}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlɪə.ɹi/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪəri|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# [[cautious|Cautious]], [[suspicious]], [[wary]], [[hesitant]], or [[nervous]] about something; having [[reservations]] or [[concern]]s.
#: ''Since he was bitten by a dog when he was young, he has always been '''leery''' of animals.''

